{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And HaShem said: I have surely seen the affliction of My people.</b> 'רָאִיתִי' connotes the past, and He likewise doubled the language of seeing. It appears that this is its meaning: for the Holy One, blessed be He, wished to give Moses a reason why He had abandoned them for such a long time, and delayed until now to look upon their trouble. Regarding this He said: because until now — even though in all their trouble they would cry out from the midst of their hard labor — all their cries were not supplication and petition before Him, blessed be He, but a cry of complaint; but they did not seek the face of HaShem until now. This is what He said: 'וַיֹּאמֶר ה׳ רָאֹה רָאִיתִי' — 'I see now,' and also 'I have seen' in the past, 'אֶת עֳנִי עַמִּי'; 'וְאֶת צַעֲקָתָם שָׁמַעְתִּי' — that is, a cry of complaint. And they did not remember that I said to Jacob, 'אָנֹכִי אֵרֵד עִמְּךָ' (Genesis 46:4), and the purpose of this descent was to save him, etc., and to bring him up, as it is written, 'וְאָנֹכִי אַעַלְךָ גַם עָלֹה' (Genesis 46:4). This is what He said: 'וָאֵרֵד לְהַצִּילוֹ' (Exodus 3:8), and they should have taken it to heart and sought My face. But now, 'צַעֲקַת בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל בָּאָה אֵלָי' (Exodus 3:9) — for they prayed to Me with a whole heart; therefore I have seen their prayer. 'וְגַם רָאִיתִי אֶת הַלַּחַץ אֲשֶׁר מִצְרַיִם לֹחֲצִים אֹתָם' (Exodus 3:9) — beyond what was lawful. Therefore, 'וְעַתָּה לְכָה וְאֶשְׁלָחֲךָ אֶל פַּרְעֹה' (Exodus 3:10) — now, immediately, for such is My way: 'עוֹד הֵם מְדַבְּרִים וַאֲנִי אֶשְׁמָע' (Isaiah 65:24)."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:18:09.779366502Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}